  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Technical Assistance - Khayelitsha And Mitchells Plain Digital Inclusion, through Government of South Africa</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This $315,000 feasibility study grant supported an evaluation of the technical, financial, and other critical aspects of extending Cape Town&apos;s municipal optic fiber backbone to and implementing a Wi-Fi network in two of the municipality&apos;s townships, Khayelitsha and Mitchells Plain. The implementation of a Wi-Fi network in these townships would significantly increase residents&apos; access to affordable, reliable telecommunication services.</narrative>
  </description>
